Ratio2pH mathematical extraction and local NumPy adaptation

Original author: Ann-Kathrin Roessling and collaborators, Ratio2pH.
Source software: Ratio2pH v3.0, Zenodo record18460719, Creative Commons
Attribution4.0 International, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18460719 .
The released Ratio2pH.py is byte-identical to the identified author repository
revision. The repository has no independent root license: permission here is
the explicitly licensed software release, not an inferred repository license.
License text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode .
Changes: extracted explicit normalization, sigmoid response/inverse and float32
image storage into local NumPy functions; replaced ImageJ dialogs, TIFF IO and
LUT overlays with benchmark NPZ interfaces and maintainer plots. Core numerical
constants, inverse clipping and calibration arithmetic are preserved and tested.

Real observations: Roessling et al., BMC Methods2026, associated FreiData
dataset DOI10.60493/t29wb-7my86, Creative Commons Attribution4.0 International.
Original microscopy-ratio images, all included roots and calibration samples
are attributed to the dataset authors. Container conversion does not add
independent chemical pH truth. No endorsement is implied.
